# 📖 Learn Before You Code

## What is it?

A function can accept one or more parameters.
It can perform a task and then return a result.
This makes your code reusable and organised.

## Why do programmers use it?

Think of a calculator. You enter numbers, it performs a calculation, and gives you the answer back.

## Real-Life Example

A food delivery app receives your order details, prepares the order, and returns the delivery status.

## Important Points

- Functions can take parameters.
- They can return a value.
- Returned values can be stored in variables.
- One function can be reused many times.
- Small functions are easier to test.

> 💡 **Remember:** A returned value can be used in another part of your program.

## Common Beginner Mistake

Printing the result inside the function when the task asks you to return it.

## Tiny Summary

Functions become powerful when they accept inputs and return outputs.

